Package: bucketimpute
Type: Package
Title: Bucketed Imputation Regression (BIR)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("BIR", "Author", email = "bir@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bucketed Imputation Regression (BIR) is a regression method that
    divides the continuous response into equal-frequency quantile buckets,
    fits per-bucket linear degree-2 'earth' (MARS) imputation models (linear
    main effects plus pairwise interactions, no hinges) that reconstruct each
    predictor from the others, converts per-bucket standardized reconstruction
    error into affinity features, and fits a cross-validated lasso of the
    response on those affinities. Predictions return a point estimate plus a
    simple affinity-weighted heteroscedastic scale. This implementation uses
    the 'lars' package for the cross-validated lasso (selecting the penalty at
    minimum cross-validated MSE) instead of 'glmnet'; see the function
    documentation for details of this deliberate substitution.
